# Recognition Pipeline Architecture

## Overview

The recognition pipeline is a two-stage producer-consumer system that runs when the
battle-assist toggle (`IsBattleAssistEnabled`) is turned ON. It consists of:

1. **Capture Thread** — continuously screenshots the game window.
2. **Detection Thread** — reads the latest screenshot, runs YOLO inference, publishes results.

Both threads communicate through **shared state objects** that any number of consumer
threads (auto-dodge, auto-skill, debug UI, etc.) can read without coordination with
each other.

```
┌─────────────┐   Update(bitmap)   ┌───────────────────┐   CloneLatest()   ┌──────────────────┐
│CaptureLoop  │ ─────────────────► │SharedCaptureFrame │ ────────────────► │DetectionLoop     │
│(Task.Run)   │                    │  FrameId + Bitmap │                   │(Task.Run)        │
└─────────────┘                    └───────────────────┘                   └────────┬─────────┘
                                                                                   │
                                          Update(frameId, results)                 │
                                   ┌───────────────────┐◄──────────────────────────┘
                                   │SharedDetectionState│
                                   │  FrameId + Results │
                                   └───────────────────┘
                                          │ GetLatest()
                                          ▼
                                   ┌───────────────┐
                                   │Consumer threads│
                                   │(dodge, skill…) │
                                   └───────────────┘
```

